/--
**L4's dominance inequality for `cleared_0`, in exact `ℕ` arithmetic at `m₀ = 1120`.**
This one exact check is the whole content of the L4 row for this polynomial: each term of
`|a_i| m^i / (|a_d| m^d)` is strictly decreasing in real `m > 0`, so the criterion of
section 1 lifts it to the entire real tail.  The kernel evaluates a 510-term Horner sum
against a 831-digit leading coefficient times `1120 ^ 510`.
-/
theorem c0_dominance_nat :
    hornerN (c0low.map Int.natAbs) 1120 < c0lead.natAbs * 1120 ^ 510 := by
  decide +kernel

/--
**K-M0, in Lean.**  The same inequality FAILS at `m₀ - 1`, so `1120` is the LEAST integer the
criterion admits for `cleared_0`.  The chain-close pass ran this kill in python
(`results/log_m0.txt`); here it is checked rather than reported.
