splits into linear factors with rational roots, so it HAS roots modulo every prime; what
this certifies is that none of them falls in `[0, 1127]`.
-/
theorem c3_scan : scanNZ r3 scanP 1128 = true := by
  decide +kernel

/-- The scan, as nonvanishing at every index it covers. -/
theorem c3_ne_zero_of_lt (n : ℕ) (hn : n < 1128) : hornerZ c3 (n : ℤ) ≠ 0 :=
  hornerZ_ne_zero_of_hornerNM c3 r3 n scanP (by decide) c3_reduction
    (scanNZ_spec c3_scan n hn)

/--
**`cleared_3(n) ≠ 0` for EVERY natural `n`** -- the scan below 1128, the criterion at and
above 1127, and the two ranges overlap.  This is the finite fact the chain's `P_3` hypothesis
needs: `cleared_3 = P_3 * G`, so `cleared_3(n) ≠ 0` gives `P_3(n) ≠ 0`.
-/
theorem c3_ne_zero (n : ℕ) : hornerZ c3 (n : ℤ) ≠ 0 := by
  rcases Nat.lt_or_ge n 1128 with h | h
  · exact c3_ne_zero_of_lt n h
  · exact c3_ne_zero_of_ge n (by omega)

/--
**L9's finite residue.**  The exact `q_{1127}` produced by the chain-close propagation is
nonzero (`results/qrow_mstar.txt`, 20567 digits), which is the whole content of the L9
row's remaining hypothesis at this index.
-/
theorem q1127_ne_zero : q1127 ≠ 0 := by decide +kernel

/--
**This is NOT D3's `hrow`, and this docstring asserted that it was until 2026-09-09.**  The
retired claim read "the witness, in the shape `∃ k, m₀ ≤ k ∧ q k ≠ 0` asks for" -- but read the
statement beneath it: the second conjunct is `q1127 ≠ 0`, a FIXED constant, not `q k ≠ 0`.
Nothing under the binder depends on `k`, so `∃ k` is decoration: the statement is logically just
`q1127_ne_zero` with a trivially-satisfiable `1127 ≤ k` stapled on.  It is TRUE,
`decide +kernel`-proved and receipted -- and VACUOUS as a row-existence claim.  The docstring
named the very shape it failed to have, which is why reading the two lines together is the check
that catches it and reading either alone is not.

Why it degenerates is the part worth keeping: **there is no `q : ℕ → ℤ` in this corpus to write
`q k` with.**  What exists is the single numeral `q1127` (20567 digits) from the
chain-close propagation.  Discharging `hrow` needs that function AND a bridge from it to
`candidateM.qn`, and neither is built.  Do not cite this theorem as closing the L9 row.
-/
theorem exists_nonzero_row : ∃ k : ℕ, 1127 ≤ k ∧ q1127 ≠ 0 :=
  ⟨1127, le_refl _, q1127_ne_zero⟩

